ell\nvar outputEl = gd.closest('.output');\nif (outputEl) {{\n    x.observe(outputEl, {childList: true});\n}}\n\n                        })                };            </script>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Skill gaps\n\nRequired level is scaled from market demand: the most-demanded skill maps to 5, and others scale proportionally. A gap is the required level minus a member's level (0 if they meet it). This is a relative measure, not an absolute standard of expertise.\n\n::: {#a8f28a98 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nrequired = (demand / demand.max() * 5)\ngap = (required - df_skills[required.index]).clip(lower=0).round(1)\n\nfig = px.imshow(gap, text_auto=\".1f\", color_continuous_scale=\"Reds\",\n                aspect=\"auto\",\n                title=\"Skill Gaps vs. Market Demand (higher = bigger gap)\")\nfig.show()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display}\n```{=html}\n<div style=\"height:525px; width:100%;\">            <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/3.2.2/es5/tex-svg.min.js\"></script><script>if (window.MathJax && window.MathJax.Hub && window.MathJax.Hub.Config) {window.MathJax.Hub.Config({SVG: {font: \"STIX-Web\"}});}</script>                <script>window.PlotlyConfig = {MathJaxConfig: 'local'};</script>\n        <script charset=\"utf-8\" src=\"https://cdn.plot.ly/plotly-4.1.1.min.js\" integrity=\"sha256-O24V1F27f8pb0glCkelh3cVHLNiHAJ5gCaVtq2aNch8=\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>                <div id=\"e71caabf-63eb-42ac-a006-639a12e10bc8\" class=\"plotly-graph-div\" style=\"height:100%; width:100%;\"></div>            <script>                window.PLOTLYENV=window.PLOTLYENV || {};                                if (document.getElementById(\"e71caabf-63eb-42ac-a006-639a12e10bc8\")) {                    Plotly.newPlot(                        \"e71caabf-63eb-42ac-a006-639a12e10bc8\",                        [{\"coloraxis\":\"coloraxis\",\"name\":\"0\",\"texttemplate\":\"%{z:.1f}\",\"x\"