,[0.2222222222222222,\"#7201a8\"],[0.3333333333333333,\"#9c179e\"],[0.4444444444444444,\"#bd3786\"],[0.5555555555555556,\"#d8576b\"],[0.6666666666666666,\"#ed7953\"],[0.7777777777777778,\"#fb9f3a\"],[0.8888888888888888,\"#fdca26\"],[1.0,\"#f0f921\"]]},\"colorway\":[\"#2C7FB8\",\"#41B6C4\",\"#A1DAB4\",\"#FDAE61\",\"#D7191C\"],\"font\":{\"color\":\"#2a3f5f\",\"family\":\"Arial\",\"size\":14},\"geo\":{\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"lakecolor\":\"white\",\"landcolor\":\"white\",\"showlakes\":true,\"showland\":true,\"subunitcolor\":\"#C8D4E3\"},\"hoverlabel\":{\"align\":\"left\"},\"hovermode\":\"closest\",\"margin\":{\"b\":0,\"l\":0,\"r\":0,\"t\":30},\"paper_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"plot_bgcolor\":\"white\",\"polar\":{\"angularaxis\":{\"gridcolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"ticks\":\"\"},\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"radialaxis\":{\"gridcolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"ticks\":\"\"}},\"scene\":{\"xaxis\":{\"backgroundcolor\":\"white\",\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"gridwidth\":2,\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"showbackground\":true,\"ticks\":\"\",\"zerolinecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\"},\"yaxis\":{\"backgroundcolor\":\"white\",\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"gridwidth\":2,\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"showbackground\":true,\"ticks\":\"\",\"zerolinecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\"},\"zaxis\":{\"backgroundcolor\":\"white\",\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"gridwidth\":2,\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"showbackground\":true,\"ticks\":\"\",\"zerolinecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\"}},\"shapedefaults\":{\"line\":{\"color\":\"#2a3f5f\"}},\"ternary\":{\"aaxis\":{\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"linecolor\":\"#A2B1C6\",\"ticks\":\"\"},\"baxis\":{\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"linecolor\":\"#A2B1C6\",\"ticks\":\"\"},\"bgcolor\":\"white\",\"caxis\":{\"gridcolor\":\"#DFE8F3\",\"linecolor\":\"#A2B1C6\",\"ticks\":\"\"}},\"title\":{\"x\":0.05},\"xaxis\":{\"automargin\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"ticks\":\"\",\"title\":{\"standoff\":15},\"zerolinecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"zerolinewidth\":2},\"yaxis\":{\"automargin\":true,\"gridcolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"linecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"ticks\":\"\",\"title\":{\"standoff\":15},\"zerolinecolor\":\"#EBF0F8\",\"zerolinewidth\":2}}},\"xaxis\":{\"anchor\":\"y\",\"domain\":[0.0,1.0]},\"yaxis\":{\"anchor\":\"x\",\"domain\":[0.0,1.0],\"autorange\":\"reversed\",\"title\":{\"text\":\"Name\"}},\"coloraxis\":{\"colorscale\":[[0.0,\"rgb(255,245,240)\"],[0.125,\"rgb(254,224,210)\"],[0.25,\"rgb(252,187,161)\"],[0.375,\"rgb(252,146,114)\"],[0.5,\"rgb(251,106,74)\"],[0.625,\"rgb(239,59,44)\"],[0.75,\"rgb(203,24,29)\"],[0.875,\"rgb(165,15,21)\"],[1.0,\"rgb(103,0,13)\"]],\"autocolorscale\":false},\"title\":{\"text\":\"Skill Gaps vs. Market Demand (higher = bigger gap)\"}},                        {\"responsive\": true}                    ).then(function(){\n                            \nvar gd = document.getElementById('e71caabf-63eb-42ac-a006-639a12e10bc8');\nvar x = new MutationObserver(function (mutations, observer) {{\n        var display = window.getComputedStyle(gd).display;\n        if (!display || display === 'none') {{\n            console.log([gd, 'removed!']);\n            Plotly.purge(gd);\n            observer.disconnect();\n        }}\n}});\n\n// Listen for the removal of the full notebook cells\nvar notebookContainer = gd.closest('#notebook-container');\nif (notebookContainer) {{\n    x.observe(notebookContainer, {childList: true});\n}}\n\n// Listen for the clearing of the current output cell\nvar outputEl = gd.closest('.output');\nif (outputEl) {{\n    x.observe(outputEl, {childList: true});\n}}\n\n                        })                };            </script>        </div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#e0ca4424 .cell execution_count=5}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nsummary = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Team average\": df_skills.mean().round(1),\n    \"Market-required level\": required.round(1),\n    \"Average gap\": gap.mean().round(1),\n}).sort_values(\"Average gap\", ascending=False)\nsummary\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=5}\n```{=html}\n<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>Team average</th>\n      <th>Market-required level</th>\n      <th>Average gap</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Python</th>\n      <td>3.2</td>\n      <td>5.0</td>\n      <td>1.8</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Machine Learning</th>\n      <td>2.2</td>\n      <td>4.1</td>\n      <td>1.8</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>SQL</th>\n      <td>3.0</td>\n      <td>2.5</td>\n      <td>0.1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Cloud (AWS/Azure/GCP)</th>\n      <td>1.5</td>\n      <td>0.4</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Deep Learning</th>\n      <td>1.5</td>\n      <td>0.8</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Databricks</th>\n      <td>1.2</td>\n      <td>0.5</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Data Pipelines</th>\n      <td>1.5</td>\n      <td>0.8</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Kubernetes</th>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>0.5</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Power BI</th>\n      <td>2.0</td>\n      <td>0.4</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Statistics</th>\n      <td>3.0</td>\n      <td>1.0</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>Tableau</th>\n      <td>2.0</td>\n      <td>0.6</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>TensorFlow</th>\n      <td>1.5</td>\n      <td>1.1</td>\n      <td>0.0</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Improvement plan\n\n#### Priorities per member\n\nEach member's three largest gaps, taken from the gap heatmap above.\n\n::: {#dd4166c8 .cell execution_count=6}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntop3 = {\n    name: [s for s in row.sort_values(ascending=False).head(3).index if row[s] > 0]\n    for name, row in gap.iterrows()\n}\nlines = []\nfor name, skills in top3.items():\n    if skills:\n        items = \", \".join(f\"**{s}** (gap {gap.loc[name, s]})\" for s in skills)\n    else:\n        items = \"no gaps against the market-required levels\"\n    lines.append(f\"- **{name}:** {items}\")\ndisplay(Markdown(\"\\n\".join(lines)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n- **Richa:** **Machine Learning** (gap 1.1), **Python** (gap 1.0)\n- **James:** **Machine Learning** (gap 2.1), **Python** (gap 2.0), **TensorFlow** (gap 0.1)\n- **Ben:** **Machine Learning** (gap 1.1), **Python** (gap 1.0)\n- **Victoria:** **Machine Learning** (gap 3.1), **Python** (gap 3.0), **SQL** (gap 0.5)\n:::\n:::\n\n\n#### Resources\n\n::: {#ee29f42b .cell execution_count=7}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nresources = {\n    \"Python\": \"Kaggle Learn: Python and Pandas (free, short, hands-on)\",\n    \"SQL\": \"Kaggle Learn: Intro to SQL, then Mode's SQL Tutorial\",\n    \"Machine Learning\": \"Coursera: Machine Learning Specialization (DeepLearning.AI / Stanford)\",\n    \"Deep Learning\": \"fast.ai Practical Deep Learning, or the DeepLearning.AI Deep Learning Specialization\",\n    \"TensorFlow\": \"Official TensorFlow tutorials at tensorflow.org/tutorials\",\n    \"Data Pipelines\": \"DataTalks.Club Data Engineering Zoomcamp (free) and the Apache Airflow docs\",\n    \"Cloud (AWS/Azure/GCP)\": \"AWS Skill Builder or Microsoft Learn (free fundamentals paths)\",\n    \"Statistics\": \"Khan Academy Statistics and Probability, or a Coursera statistics course\",\n    \"Tableau\": \"Tableau Public free training videos\",\n    \"Power BI\": \"Microsoft Learn: Power BI learning paths\",\n    \"Databricks\": \"Databricks Academy free self-paced courses\",\n    \"Kubernetes\": \"Official tutorials at kubernetes.io/docs/tutorials\",\n}\npriority_skills = sorted({s for skills in top3.values() for s in skills})\nrows = [\"| Priority skill | Suggested course or resource |\", \"|---|---|\"]\nrows += [f\"| {s} | {resources.get(s, 'Official documentation')} |\" for s in priority_skills]\ndisplay(Markdown(\"\\n\".join(rows)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n| Priority skill | Suggested course or resource |\n|---|---|\n| Machine Learning | Coursera: Machine Learning Specialization (DeepLearning.AI / Stanford) |\n| Python | Kaggle Learn: Python and Pandas (free, short, hands-on) |\n| SQL | Kaggle Learn: Intro to SQL, then Mode's SQL Tutorial |\n| TensorFlow | Official TensorFlow tutorials at tensorflow.org/tutorials |\n:::\n:::\n\n\n#### Team collaboration\n\nThe strongest member on each priority skill teaches the others who need it.\n\n::: {#5f518aac .cell execution_count=8}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nlines = []\nfor s in priority_skills:\n    teacher = df_skills[s].idxmax()\n    learners = [n for n, sk in top3.items() if s in sk and n != teacher]\n    if learners:\n        lines.append(f\"- **{s}:** {teacher} (level {df_skills.loc[teacher, s]}) \"\n                     f\"leads a short session for {', '.join(learners)}.\")\ndisplay(Markdown(\"\\n\".join(lines)))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display .cell-output-markdown}\n- **Machine Learning:** Richa (level 3) leads a short session for James, Ben, Victoria.\n- **Python:** Richa (level 4) leads a short session for James, Ben, Victoria.\n- **SQL:** Richa (level 4) leads a short session for Victoria.\n- **TensorFlow:** Richa (level 2) leads a short session for James.\n:::\n:::\n\n\nTo make this work in practice, the team will hold one 30-minute skill-share each week, with the teacher walking through a small example. Members will also pair up on the project's own tasks, such as cleaning data or building a chart, so that each person practices their priority skills on real work. Finally, we will build one shared practice project on this project's market dataset and review each other's changes through GitHub before merging.\n\n",
